BOB-190 — the documented test command could not run. Fixed at the docs layer.
captured: 2026-08-25T20:29:07Z

THE DEFECT: CLAUDE.md documented 'python3 -m pytest tests/unit/ ...' as canonical, and
that command could not execute at all.

--- BEFORE (the command CLAUDE.md told you to type) ---
$ python3 -m pytest tests/unit/merge_service/ -q --import-mode=importlib --co
  File "/home/milosvasic/.local/lib/python3/site-packages/rpds/__init__.py", line 1
    from .rpds import *
ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'rpds.rpds'

--- AFTER (the command CLAUDE.md documents now) ---
$ .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/merge_service/ -q --import-mode=importlib --co
883 tests collected in 1.99s

ROOT CAUSE, measured not inferred: ~/.local/lib/python3/site-packages ships
_pydantic_core.cpython-313-x86_64-linux-gnu.so — a cp313 ABI binary — under a Python
3.14.6 interpreter. Same for rpds_py. That directory is the HOST-WIDE 'pip install
--user' tree shared with aider, bandit, asciinema and others, all pinned to those cp313
builds. It is NOT .venv, which is unaffected: .venv carries pydantic_core 2.46.4 /
fastapi 0.141.1 and imports cleanly.

WHY THE DOCS FIX IS THE RIGHT ONE HERE, not a workaround:
  - scripts/run-tests.sh ALREADY selects .venv/bin/python — the working path predates
    this item and is what the project actually runs.
  - docs/TESTING.md ALREADY documents '.venv/bin/python -m pytest' (2 occurrences).
    CLAUDE.md was the SOLE remaining place naming the broken interpreter, so this is
    an internal-consistency repair, not a new convention.
  - Repairing the host tree would touch state shared by unrelated tools and is outside
    this repository entirely.

DECIDED AUTONOMOUSLY under §11.4.101: reversible (a one-line-per-line doc edit),
determinable from captured evidence (the two runs above), bounded blast radius (a
documentation string), and it aligns three sources that already disagreed. The
alternative — repairing host site-packages — remains available to the operator and is
NOT foreclosed by this closure; it is simply not boba's to do.

HONEST BOUNDARY (§11.4.6): the host interpreter is still broken for anything that
imports FastAPI through it. Nothing in this repository now points anyone at it, but
this closure does not repair the host and does not claim to.

§11.4.238 coverage-escape note: this was found out-of-band by an agent, not by any
automated check. No gate asserts that the commands our own documentation prints can
actually execute. That gap is real and is recorded here rather than closed silently.
